# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# RC Rally Hub — Environment Variables (example)
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development, and add the same
# keys in Netlify: Site settings → Environment variables.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit a real `.env` file. Never reference secret
# keys directly in frontend/browser code — only inside Netlify
# Functions (server-side), which is what these are reserved for.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Future: Netlify Functions integrations (server-side only) ---
# Booking itself is handled by the separate `bookingsystem` project (see
# its own .env.example) — these are placeholders for anything else this
# site's frontend might eventually need a secret-holding backend for.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# SMS_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# --- Future: OpenAI-powered chatbot upgrade (server-side only, called
# from a Netlify Function — never exposed to the browser) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Optional analytics / maps ---
# PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_EMBED_SRC=

# --- Turso (libSQL) database ---
# Leave both unset (or point TURSO_DATABASE_URL at a file: path) for local
# development -- src/lib/db.ts then opens db/local.db automatically and no
# Turso account is needed. Set both to switch to a real hosted database
# (create one at https://turso.tech, then `turso db show <name> --url` and
# `turso db tokens create <name>`):
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db-name.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Admin portal login/session auth needs no separate secret here — session
# tokens are opaque random values, hashed and validated against the
# `admin_sessions` table in the same database (see src/lib/auth.ts).
